6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8637313167">May 28, 2026</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">4⭐️<blockquote>"Fortune favors the brave. But the stars smile upon those who are true to their hearts."</blockquote> This was a great farewell to the Bridge Kingdom series. I've been reading these since the beginning and honestly couldn't see how DJ was going to wrap everything up in one book but alas, she pulled it off!<br /><br />I'm going to join every other review in saying that before things for our characters get good here, they get REALLY bad. Like we open up from the end of The Twisted Throne with shit hitting the fan and that really just snowballs for the rest of the book. <br /><br />This series has gotten heavier on the politics as it's progressed and this book is no exception. Almost too much in my opinion- I understand why all of it was necessary but I do think it weighed the story down a bit. Having to see our characters do something and then have four other povs hear about that event but from different sources and interpret them differently and try to figure out the schemes involved was a bit exhausting. Like every character here learned about King Edward's death, had their own opinions, then those would change with new information, they would get at <i>why/i&gt; it happened, change those opinions again. At a certain point I just wanted to get on with it. <br /><br />This book also made me try and question the population of Ithicana. Because seriously, how many mass casualty events can those people go through in one series and still have warriors ready to fight!?</i></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">13 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.66834148,18.1034086 C9.31027068,18.6437214 8.696742,19 8,19 L6,19 C4.8954305,19 4,18.1045695 4,17 L4,12 C4,10.8954305 4.8954305,10 