show/8611617725">May 25, 2026</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">4.25 stars<br /><br />This was a pretty satisfying end to the series.<br /><br />From page one until the very end, the pace was nonstop, which I personally really enjoy. This last book brought all six main character POVs, so there was always something crazy going on.<br /><br />My final verdict on the James storyline carrying over from the previous book is 👎🏻<br />He didn't do nearly enough, nothing really, to make up for his utter stupidity and betrayal of Ahnna. Circumstances just forced them back together and it seemed it was more for survival that they just moved on from everything because so much else was going on.<br /><br />But the story was so engaging, and I was thinking I could look past James enough to maybe rate this 5 stars, but the every single protagonist CONSTANTLY on the back foot got old real fast. <br /><br />Every single character got manipulated so horribly so constantly, and not once did they ever learn from it. The heros coming out on top just really seemed the purest form of luck and the antagonists fucking some stuff up.<br /><br />But all that aside, this book was epic, tense, emotional, and a mostly satisfying end to everyone's stories 💜</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">9 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter