Text"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">⭐ <b>2/5 Stars</b><br /><br /><b>How does a series I once considered a favorite end with me wanting to rip this book into pieces?</b><br /><br />I genuinely don’t know how I went from: <b>“This series is brilliant”</b><br /><br />…to sitting here after <i>The Tempest Blade</i> feeling nothing but:<br /><br />* rage<br />* frustration<br />* exhaustion<br />* and disappointment.<br /><br />Because WHAT was this ending???<br /><br />First of all: <b>748 pages.</b><br /><br />SEVEN. HUNDRED. FORTY. EIGHT.<br /><br />And somehow this book still felt like:<br /><br />* repetitive chaos<br />* endless defeat<br />* and characters continuously making the dumbest possible decisions.<br /><br />I truly need to know what the editor was doing here because this desperately needed tightening. It honestly felt like everyone collectively decided: <i>“It’s the final book, let the author do whatever she wants.”</i><br /><br />And unfortunately… that ambition completely spiraled out of control.<br /><br />The biggest issue with this book is that Danielle L. Jensen became so obsessed with creating villains who were supposedly: <b>“too smart to defeat”</b><br /><br />…that she accidentally made every single protagonist look completely incompetent.<br /><br />And I mean EVERYONE.<br /><br />We had six main characters<br /><br />…and somehow not a single functioning brain cell between all six of them combined.<br /><br />For over <b>600 pages</b>, these people just:<br /><br />* lose<br />* get manipulated<br />* get captured<br />* get outsmarted<br />* walk into obvious traps<br />* repeat.<br /><br />Over and over and OVER again.<br /><br />And then suddenly in the final hundred pages: <b>fate fixes everything.</b><br /><br />No. Absolutely not.<br /><br />That’s not clever plotting. That’s narrative exhaustion.<br /><br />And don’t even get me started on the plot holes.<br /><br />Because PLEASE explain to me why, after Alexandra literally confesses publicly to all her crimes and atrocities, James doesn’t simply: <b>claim the throne and end the war immediately?</b><br /><br />You know why?<br /><br />Because the author needed, one more war, one more hopeless battle, one more dramatic “all is lost” moment, one more last-second save.<br /><br />It became so repetitive that by the end I was rolling my eyes and skimming through the pages to end my misery.<br /><br />And Ahnna?<br /><br /><b>THE DUMBEST FMC IN THIS ENTIRE SERIES.</b><br /><br />I tried. I truly tried with her.<br /><br />But this woman is supposedly:<br /><br />* a hardened soldier<br />* brutal in battle<br />* capable of slaughtering enemies without hesitation<br /><br />…and yet suddenly loses every ounce of survival instinct when it actually matters???<br /><br />The entire situation with Lestara made me want to scream.<br /><br />Because somehow THIS woman: <b>Lestara.</b><br /><br />…ends up being the mastermind-level villain who outplays kingdoms, manipulates everyone, and sparks wars across multiple countries.<br /><br />And then Ahnna:<br /><br />* lets herself get captured<br />* jumps into shark-infested waters<br />* risks everything to save Lestara’s baby<br /><br />…because apparently this child is destined to bring about some golden era???<br /><br /><b>Excuse me?</b><br /><br />So according to this story:<br />the child of two objectively terrible people is somehow a better future ruler than James and Ahnna?<br /><br />I genuinely cannot.<br /><br />And the most frustrating part?<br />The only reason this book gets ANY stars from me is because of the older characters I already loved:<br />Lara, Aren, Zarrah &amp; Keris.<br /><br />Though honestly even Zarrah and Keris started irritating me here because HOW are you still getting trapped and manipulated this late in the game??<br /><br />For all of Keris’s endless speeches about how intelligent and strategic he is, the man got outplayed repeatedly by two women while acting shocked every single time 😭<br /><br />Meanwhile Lara and Aren?<br />Still my babies. Still superior to everyone else in this series.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">6 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.66834148,18.1034086 C9.31027068,18.6437214 8.696742,19 8,19 L6,19 C4.8954305,19 4,18.1045695 4,17 L4,12 C4,10.8954305 4.8954305,10 6,10 L8,10 C8.60249245,10 9.14276174,10.2664091 9.50943372,10.6878531