rWyPkPAQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:172236858"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785657601646,"createdAt":1784398353244,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1785583874890,"text":"\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003cu\u003einfinite stars\u003c/u\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e!!!!!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003etruly the end of an era. and to no one's surprise, i cried.\u003cbr /\u003ethis is why i read fantasy.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003erandom lore drop, i first read bridge kingdom back around 2020-21. it was one of first fantasy books that i'd read. in fact this series got me into reading fantasy. dlj is one of my autobuy authors and this book reminded me exactly why.\u003cbr /\u003ei've given ALL books in this series 5 stars. and this one was no exception. the romance, plot twists, conflicts, tension, political intrigue, and then the resolution? everything delivered sbbb. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003ci\u003ethe stakes were high but their ambition was even higher. \u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cu\u003ewhat a fantastic way to end a series.\u003c/u\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ei wish i could read this series for the first time again. i hate that i will never be able to read this series for the first time ever again💔😭😭😭\u003cbr /\u003edespite being over 750 pages long, it was so fast paced. my heart was racing sb i was worried it would fall out of my chest. i was worried sick because the stakes were SO high. just when you think that the mc's have it under their control, dlj throws ANOTHER curveball which will leave your jaw dropping to the floor. if you know me, you probably know that i love political fantasy. and this book did NOT disappoint. idt i've ever read a fantasy series that handles political intrigue this well. i never saw the plot twists coming. it was just curveballs after another😭 also, this book had 6 pov's. aren, lara, zarrah, keris and ahnna, james. elite decision imo. their decisions were so interconnected and their stories were so intertwined. everyone had an important role to play and all 750 pages were well worth it. this book provides more depth to the court politics, and not just of one or two nations that was previously seen in the last 5 books. but all 6 kingdoms in this world. the north and south kingdoms. and yet, bridge kingdom remains in the center of it all. every moment in the last 5 books led to this epic finale and it was so bittersweet. \u003cbr /\u003eit gave the characters (and me) the closure that i desperately needed. though i wouldn't mind if dlj decides to write their children's books next (please do😭😭😭i need more of this world i can't let go of them yet. all 6 of them have my whole heart) \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003cu\u003eall in all, everything just came full circle. \u003c/u\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ei don't know what else to say without spoiling anything, but what i do know is that if you love fantasy/romantasy, bridge kingdom series is a must read and is not the one to be missed🤍\u003cbr /\u003e(\u003cs\u003ealso, i read book 5 and book 6 in less than 24 hours but if even that doesn't convince you, tbh, i dont know what else will\u003c/s\u003e 😭😭😭😭)","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AMJQZ4QE0FRTP\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}"},"likeCount":174,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":38},"User:87641270":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":87641270,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1756049671i/87641270._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":4,"textReviewsCount":142,"name":"avalon","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/87641270-avalon","contributor":null,"id":87641270},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AD2XCE0RZ6XPJ":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AD2XCE0RZ6XPJ"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.UhwB