:{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}"},"likeCount":10,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:33595199":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":33595199,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1737507415i/33595199._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":0,"textReviewsCount":99,"name":"\u0026#x1d62b;\u0026#x1d622;\u0026#x1d634; ♡","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/33595199-x1d62b-x1d622-x1d634","contributor":null,"id":33595199},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1TTGRG8ODN39P":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TTGRG8ODN39P"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TTGRG8ODN39P\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1TTGRG8ODN39P","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TTGRG8ODN39P"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/33595199?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8446745273"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.lUgGV6yEqlZ0Uy5eHapyXA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.lUgGV6yEqlZ0Uy5eHapyXA","creator":{"__ref":"User:33595199"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1778462229824,"createdAt":1777243821277,"spoilerStatus":true,"lastRevisionAt":1777243829243,"text":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\"As someone who \u003ci\u003eis\u003c/i\u003e a murderer, I say with the utmost confidence that Ahnna didn't do this. She's being framed, and my gut tells me that Alexandra is at the center of it.\"\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eCan all books be about Lara Veliant?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eGenuinely. Because I fucking love her. And she proves CONSTANTLY how much that love is warranted. She’s not just a badass, she’s also so fucking smart she saw through Alexandra’s frame job instantly. Some may call her overpowered; I call her the best fmc I’ve ever read. Argue with the wall.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI’m pleased to note, as an aside, that I’m also significantly more fond of Keris in this book than I have been previously. So that’s a major plus because bro has hella screen time—it would have been intolerable if I hated him.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut seriously, you can tell he’s the author’s favorite character. We spend so much unnecessary time in his POV, and it’s all very clearly just fan service. His chapters (excessive in number and needlessly lengthy) weigh the plot down and make the story \u003ci\u003edrag.\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI can’t deny that they’re ultimately worth it because we also get Lara and Aren’s POVs. And I might never see them again so I’ll take what I can get. But painstakingly, I must confess that their POVs contribute to the sluggish pace. Most of it would have worked better as a bonus novella, leaving this book to focus on Ahnna and James’s story. Because by the last like 20%, while I simultaneously didn’t want to part with Lara and Aren forever, I was more than ready for the book to just end already.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnyway.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhen it came to Aren hunting down Lara, there was never a single moment where I even half believed that when he found her, he could kill her. With James, it’s much different. Because the romance was so underdeveloped in the previous books, I have no difficulty—or even a hint of a problem—accepting the idea that James would kill her the second he found her. That being a false belief—if he could kill her, it wouldn’t be much of a romance—doesn’t help much, because I don’t feel any emotional weight holding him back, and I should.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eHe cast his eyes skyward. \"Keep this up, Princess, and you'll make Carlo's job easier.\"\u003cbr /\u003e\"Kiss my ass.\"\u003cbr /\u003e\"Bend over.\"\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI know this is supposed to come off as playful banter, but after everything he did, I’m irritated by his audacity, not charmed. He should be groveling in guilt, not acting so shameless and sure of himself. More frustrating still, that comment made her blush. I really hate when a romance skips steps because they just \u003ci\u003ecan’t resist\u003c/i\u003e each other.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThey’re kissing and he’s telling her he wants her and loves her, and she’s saying they can’t be together because they stand on different sides of the war. They should be confronting the remnants of betrayal that linger between them. He should be thinking about how badly he hurt her (before \u003ci\u003eand\u003c/i\u003e after his father was killed) instead of her long, long legs, and then he should be giving her an apology he actually means.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eCan you believe Ahnna is the first (and only) one to apologize?\u003c/b\u003e Absolutely ridiculous.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eAren had not missed the mark in his assessment of James's sentiment when he'd crossed paths with the pair in Verwyrd, but it struck Lara that what had been between the two then had grown tenfold in the time since. Love, sure and true, and it hurt Lara's own heart to know that both would suffer for it.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe story constantly reaffirms how undeniably in love Ahnna and James are, but I fear I fail to see what Lara sees. I just think their relationship needed to be more emotionally fleshed out than it was for me to really believe what the book was trying to sell me. This could have been a five-star read. I almost thought it would be.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI already touched on this, but I still think we got past the him-hunting-her-down-without-hearing-her-out part way too easily. Being captured and tortured will do that to you, I guess (lol), but at least a conversation would have been nice.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThat’s not to say I wasn’t invested, because I was. I think they complemented each other quite well, and there was a lot about their relationship that I loved, like how he stood up to Aren for her. I just wanted more than what I got.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eOther brief side notes:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e* I was so happy with Ahnna and Lara’s reconciliation scene. Now that I have their sisterhood, I’m mad I didn’t have it for longer.\u003cbr /\u003e* I was so right in my review of the last book to say that I hate Georgie and Ahnna should have just killed him. She would have saved everybody a whole lot of grief.\u003cbr /\u003e* The plot with the warring kingdoms and all their moving parts finally coming together was done very well, and resulted in a wonderfully satisfying conclusion. The plot armor was definitely shiny, but I didn’t really mind.\u003cbr /\u003e* I loved the undercurrent of Sarhina dissolving the Maridrinian monarchy in favor of an elected government. It’s a small hint at meaningful reform, which I really enjoyed. Jensen is great at layering complex political dynamics beneath the surface of her narratives, and it truly elevates them to a whole new level.\u003cbr /\u003e* Can this bitch Lestara just die?\u003cbr /\u003e* The scene where Aren saved Ahnna from the gallows with his flawless aim was \u003ci\u003eincredible.\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e* The epilogue was EVVEERRYTHINGGG, I loved absolutely every second of it\u003cbr /\u003e* It makes me giddy on the inside that Aren is slightly taller than James hahahaha\u003cbr /\u003e* Did Nana seriously have to die bruh\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAlso: \u003cbr /\u003eI was eating dinner when I got to the scene with that weird psycho Carlo dude kissing Ahnna on the cheek every two seconds, and I literally had to stop eating until it was over because it was making me nauseous.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhat does it say about me that Carlo’s death was like the most distressing moment of this book for me? I wrote my reaction above in the moment, after which I found myself growing accidentally fond of Carlo’s deranged ass and his absolutely unhinged behavior.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI was holding out hope for his survival until the very end—when James slit his throat—and even then I waited an extra beat for the book to pull a last-second fake-out. He would have made life quite difficult for our main characters, so I understand why he had to die. But I’m still mourning him. :(\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e- - - - -\u003cbr /\u003eImagine my utter shock and subsequent delight when I opened the table of contents to find that Lara \u0026amp; Aren narrate a significant portion of this.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eUnfortunately, there’s also Keris’s perspective, which I will \u003cs\u003egladly\u003c/s\u003e suffer through for LAREN MY BABIES","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1TTGRG8ODN39P\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}"},"likeCount":9,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":4},"User:11845085":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":11845085,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1720121008i/11845085._UX200_CR0,20,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":717,"textReviewsCount":709,"name":"✨⚡  Kelcey (felinebooktrovert) ✨","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/11845085-kelcey-felinebooktrovert","contributor":null,"id":11845085},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2WN9T6UTFJW32":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2WN9T6UTFJW32"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2WN9T6UTFJW32\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2WN9T6UTFJW32","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2WN9T6UTFJW32"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/11845085?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8611617725"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.h0V0pqkN5LoI3YE6oika3Q":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.h0V0pqkN5LoI3YE6oika3Q","creator":{"__ref":"User:11845085"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1779688249819,"createdAt":1779673576528,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1779676324887,"text":"4.25 stars\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis was a pretty satisfying end to the series.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFrom page one until the very end, the pace was nonstop, which I personally really enjoy. This last book brought all six main character POVs, so there was always something crazy going on.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMy final verdict on the James storyline carrying over from the previous book is 👎🏻\u003cbr /\u003eHe didn't do nearly enough, nothing really, to make up for his utter stupidity and betrayal of Ahnna. Circumstances just forced them back together and it seemed it was more for survival that they just moved on from everything because so much else was going on.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut the story was so engaging, and I was thinking I could look past James enough to maybe rate this 5 stars, but the every single protagonist CONSTANTLY on the back foot got old real fast. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eEvery single character got manipulated so horribly so constantly, and not once did they ever learn from it. The heros coming out on top just really seemed the purest form of luck and the antagonists fucking some stuff up.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut all that aside, this book was epic, tense, emotional, and a mostly satisfying end to everyone's stories 💜","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2WN9T6UTFJW32\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}"},"likeCount":9,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:169974392":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":169974392,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1742726144i/169974392._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":6,"textReviewsCount":272,"name":"Mari","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/169974392-mari","contributor":null,"id":169974392},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3TFMMYQ8BI03G":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3TFMMYQ8BI03G"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3TFMMYQ8BI03G\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3TFMMYQ8BI03G","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3TFMMYQ8BI03G"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/169974392?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8537105699"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.zR6E5UrD4o6NAPboixdvZg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.zR6E5UrD4o6NAPboixdvZg","creator":{"__ref":"User:169974392"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1780577869756,"createdAt":1777476006491,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1777476016681,"text":"Million stars ⭐️\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNo notes. This book delivered.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI’m a huge fan of Danielle at this point, I’ll read anything she writes, honestly. Her duets are everything to me. She always gives you what you didn’t even realise you were missing in the first book.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis one had it all, tension, high stakes, scheming, politics, and those little moments of romance… from all the couples. And the fact that the final book was multi-POV? Love, love, loved it!!!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI have all these characters in my heart, and while I’m sad it’s over, I’m also happy that everyone got their happy ending and that peace was finally made between all the countries.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI also read the acknowledgements, and it’s wild to think that back in 2017 no one wanted to publish this because “adult fantasy” supposedly wasn’t a thing. I’m so glad Audible gave it a chance, and I’m so happy to have these books on my shelves 🩷🩷","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3TFMMYQ8BI03G\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}"},"likeCount":9,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:7027484":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":7027484,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1609257332i/7027484._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":999,"textReviewsCount":419,"name":"Sandra","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/7027484-sandra","contributor":null,"id":7027484},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2TZ5IDQ5UD51D":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2TZ5IDQ5UD51D"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2TZ5IDQ5UD51D\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2TZ5IDQ5UD51D","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2TZ5IDQ5UD51D"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/7027484?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8054080567"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.RYW3VcRhncdlGgluTlJYQw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.RYW3VcRhncdlGgluTlJYQw","creator":{"__ref":"User:7027484"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1768622542183,"createdAt":1763018434992,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1763018447930,"text":"i actually really love this world and its characeters, this was a love letter to all the other couples from the past. was it necessary? probably not but i got keris's POV again so i won't complain 😂","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2TZ5IDQ5UD51D\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}"},"likeCount":8,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.HWU5lUOJCfwaHLP54HHeNg":{"__typename":"Contributor","id":"kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.HWU5lUOJCfwaHLP54HHeNg","works":{"__typename":"ContributorWorksConnection","totalCount":2}},"User:54826165":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":54826165,"imageUrlSquare":"","isAuthor":true,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":52,"textReviewsCount":2409,"name":"Sifa Poulton","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/54826165-sifa-poulton","contributor":{"__ref":"Contributor:kca://author/amzn1.gr.author.v1.HWU5lUOJCfwaHLP54HHeNg"},"id":54826165},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AVP4MT8ILAVIA":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AVP4MT8ILAVIA"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AVP4MT8ILAVIA\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AVP4MT8ILAVIA","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AVP4MT8ILAVIA"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/54826165?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7979041827"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.QIEr9T5Uujwr6AZUEr41mw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.QIEr9T5Uujwr6AZUEr41mw","creator":{"__ref":"User:54826165"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1778287132487,"createdAt":1760131110993,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1760131112433,"text":"THE TEMPEST BLADE is an epic finale to the series.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eGiven this is the sixth - and final - book to such a successful series, and one that's had an increasingly interconnected world and complex plots, there was a lot to live up to. It had to tie up five previous books of plots and character development and send it all off in a way that's satisfying and climactic enough - while also not tipping into the realms of unbelievable. Luckily, THE TEMPEST BLADE manages that.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhile Ahnna and James are the focus, for the first time in the series, they are not the only narrators. All the narrators across the series are back for this finale - yup, all six. The story just has such a massive scope that Ahnna and James alone couldn't tell it. They only see part of this epic, final struggle for the future of Ithicana. There are schemes upon schemes, decisions from previous books bearing out their consequences for good or bad, and everyone is forced to decide how much blood is too much for one land.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ePlus, it was so nice to end with all of them speaking. Keris is the most present of the other narrators (as he's much closer to the thrust of the action). The others are also there, but Aren and Lara do speak quite a bit less so it's very nice when they are the narrators - they're the pair who kickstarted the entire series, after all.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWith so many narrators (and so much plot!) it is, unsurprisingly, a rather long book (26hrs audio - which is apparently going to end up around 800 pages in print). Despite this, I flew threw it (and actually kept cranking up the speed so I could find out what was going to happen faster! I usually listen on 1.5x but by the end I was at 2x.)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIn all, this is a really good send off to this action packed, epic series. I'll be sad to leave this world behind, but these characters could really do with a break!","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AVP4MT8ILAVIA\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}"},"likeCount":7,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:170687782":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":170687782,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1710867572i/170687782._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":0,"textReviewsCount":36,"name":"Alex","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/170687782-alex","contributor":null,"id":170687782},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2NGJE1NYMS4M1":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2NGJE1NYMS4M1"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2NGJE1NYMS4M1\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2NGJE1NYMS4M1","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2NGJE1NYMS4M1"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/170687782?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7130111939"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.DfsX26sTDfcsakrsvqzCWQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.DfsX26sTDfcsakrsvqzCWQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:170687782"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1777554208429,"createdAt":1760340937766,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1760341888154,"text":"The levels of anxiety I have when reading books from this series needs to be studied!😭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe cliff hanger of the 5th book was borderline unforgivable… I waited SO long for this book and it did not disappoint!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis series just gets better and better and the stakes get higher and higher with each book. This final one was no exception! It was so chaotic (in a good way) from beginning to end and I loved every minute of it! I also loved that it had multiple POVs! \u003cbr /\u003eAren \u0026amp; Lara were my fav couple up until James \u0026amp; Ahnna’s story began in the 5th book, so getting to hear from their perspectives again, I was over the moon happy about.🥰 There is definitely no love lost for Keris \u0026amp; Zarrah either, I was so happy to hear from their perspectives too! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis series as a whole will forever be one of my favorites and I highly recommend to anyone who loves the Romantasy genre to give it a try! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eCan’t wait for the physical copy of this book to be released because I NEED my book trophy for my shelf!","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2NGJE1NYMS4M1\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}"},"likeCount":7,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:158111410":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":158111410,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1683843272i/158111410._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":2,"textReviewsCount":44,"name":"Stephanie","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/158111410-stephanie","contributor":null,"id":158111410},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AZKXLYX9DR5K5":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AZKXLYX9DR5K5"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AZKXLYX9DR5K5\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AZKXLYX9DR5K5","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AZKXLYX9DR5K5"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/158111410?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7718394234"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.oxuK5MqK5OvAHPs9qP5WMw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.oxuK5MqK5OvAHPs9qP5WMw","creator":{"__ref":"User:158111410"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785001403787,"createdAt":1761569413596,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1761571586318,"text":"I liked the multiple POVs but I would have preferred more Aren and Lara. I LOVED the first two books of this series. I would recommend reading the first two, and then calling it there. ","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AZKXLYX9DR5K5\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.u_NuFhoiUh_Rp4N3\"}}"},"likeCount":7,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:195409939":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":195409939,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1774758623i/195409939._UX200_CR0,33,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":17,"textReviewsCount":312,"name":"Geeky Author","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/195409939-geeky-author","contributor":null,"id":195409939},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1Y3SCFD6BUXDC":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Y3SCFD6BUXDC"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Y3SCFD6BUXDC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1Y3SCFD6BUXDC","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Y3SCFD6BUXDC"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/195409939?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8600329657"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.29BJvJUz2F1610gHFtevRw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.29BJvJUz2F1610gHFtevRw","creator":{"__ref":"User:195409939"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1782623328806,"createdAt":1778800366333,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1778800546153,"text":"⭐ \u003cb\u003e2/5 Stars\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eHow does a series I once considered a favorite end with me wanting to rip this book into pieces?\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI genuinely don’t know how I went from: \u003cb\u003e“This series is brilliant”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e…to sitting here after \u003ci\u003eThe Tempest Blade\u003c/i\u003e feeling nothing but:\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e* rage\u003cbr /\u003e* frustration\u003cbr /\u003e* exhaustion\u003cbr /\u003e* and disappointment.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBecause WHAT was this ending???\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFirst of all: \u003cb\u003e748 pages.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSEVEN. HUNDRED. FORTY. EIGHT.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd somehow this book still felt like:\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e* repetitive chaos\u003cbr /\u003e* endless defeat\u003cbr /\u003e* and characters continuously making the dumbest possible decisions.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI truly need to know what the editor was doing here because this desperately needed tightening. It honestly felt like everyone collectively decided: \u003ci\u003e“It’s the final book, let the author do whatever she wants.”\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd unfortunately… that ambition completely spiraled out of control.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe biggest issue with this book is that Danielle L. Jensen became so obsessed with creating villains who were supposedly: \u003cb\u003e“too smart to defeat”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e…that she accidentally made every single protagonist look completely incompetent.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd I mean EVERYONE.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe had six main characters\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e…and somehow not a single functioning brain cell between all six of them combined.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFor over \u003cb\u003e600 pages\u003c/b\u003e, these people just:\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e* lose\u003cbr /\u003e* get manipulated\u003cbr /\u003e* get captured\u003cbr /\u003e* get outsmarted\u003cbr /\u003e* walk into obvious traps\u003cbr /\u003e* repeat.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOver and over and OVER again.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd then suddenly in the final hundred pages: \u003cb\u003efate fixes everything.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNo. Absolutely not.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThat’s not clever plotting. That’s narrative exhaustion.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd don’t even get me started on the plot holes.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBecause PLEASE explain to me why, after Alexandra literally confesses publicly to all her crimes and atrocities, James doesn’t simply: \u003cb\u003eclaim the throne and end the war immediately?\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eYou know why?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBecause the author needed, one more war, one more hopeless battle, one more dramatic “all is lost” moment, one more last-second save.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIt became so repetitive that by the end I was rolling my eyes and skimming through the pages to end my misery.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd Ahnna?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eTHE DUMBEST FMC IN THIS ENTIRE SERIES.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI tried. I truly tried with her.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBut this woman is supposedly:\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e* a hardened soldier\u003cbr /\u003e* brutal in battle\u003cbr /\u003e* capable of slaughtering enemies without hesitation\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e…and yet suddenly loses every ounce of survival instinct when it actually matters???\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe entire situation with Lestara made me want to scream.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBecause somehow THIS woman: \u003cb\u003eLestara.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e…ends up being the mastermind-level villain who outplays kingdoms, manipulates everyone, and sparks wars across multiple countries.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd then Ahnna:\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e* lets herself get captured\u003cbr /\u003e* jumps into shark-infested waters\u003cbr /\u003e* risks everything to save Lestara’s baby\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e…because apparently this child is destined to bring about some golden era???\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eExcuse me?\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSo according to this story:\u003cbr /\u003ethe child of two objectively terrible people is somehow a better future ruler than James and Ahnna?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI genuinely cannot.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd the most frustrating part?\u003cbr /\u003eThe only reason this book gets ANY stars from me is because of the older characters I already loved:\u003cbr /\u003eLara, Aren, Zarrah \u0026amp; Keris.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThough honestly even Zarrah and Keris started irritating me here because HOW are you still getting trapped and manipulated this late in the game??\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFor all of Keris’s endless speeches about how intelligent and strategic he is, the man got outplayed repeatedly by two women while acting shocked every single time 😭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMeanwhile Lara and Aren?\u003cbr /\u003eStill my babies. Still superior to everyone else in this series.","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1Y3SCFD6BUXDC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LpcMWCLKPKNoeidW\"}}"},"likeCount":6,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:162213321":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":162213321,"imageUrlSquare":"https: